00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,730
Hello, I'm Neil and I'm Georgie.

2
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:05,130
Welcome to Real easy English.

3
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:11,910
You can find a worksheet and transcript for this episode on our website, BBC Learning English dot com.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,910
Hello, Neil, how are you doing, I'm very well.

5
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:23,970
Thank you, Georgie, How are you, Yes, I'm very well.

6
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:28,710
Thank you, Neil, today, we're talking about cities.

7
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:33,450
We both live and work in London, which is a very big city.

8
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,110
It is.

9
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:36,270
It's a huge city.

10
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:38,610
Very busy and bustling.

11
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:45,750
Bustling means there's lots of activity, lots of things going on.

12
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:52,240
Speaking of what do you like about living in a big bustling city?

13
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:58,060
Well, there are lots of good things about living in a big city.

14
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,740
It's convenient.

15
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,060
It's very convenient.

16
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:15,310
So there is lots of public transport, which is sometimes good and you can get things that you need quite easily.

17
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:16,460
That's very true.

18
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:20,720
Yeah, Yeah, there's also a lot of things to do.

19
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:27,200
We are lucky in London to have lots of theatres where you can see plays.

20
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:33,790
There's a really good music scene so you can watch and listen to a lot of live music.

21
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:40,090
If you have no plans on a day, you can always find plans, spontaneous plans.

22
00:01:40,090 --> 00:01:41,710
So we are really lucky.

23
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:55,210
In that sense, yeah, and if you like art, there's all kinds of exhibitions and galleries and museums, lots of good things, but there are obviously.

24
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:58,460
Some bad things about living in a city aren't there.

25
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:08,720
Yes, do you want to tell us some, Yeah, well, it's very noisy and dirty and busy and expensive.

26
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:22,760
It's always more expensive in a big city, especially the capital city, so you can do all of the things that we just talked about, but you have to pay.

27
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:36,490
And things like eating out, especially going for a drink, is really expensive thing to do in a capital city I feel like every time I leave the house, I just spend loads of money.

28
00:02:36,510 --> 00:02:39,060
And that is quite frustrating.

29
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:42,180
But you have to pay for good, for good times.

30
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:47,520
I guess, yeah, have you ever lived in another city apart from London.

31
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:48,770
Yes, I have.

32
00:02:48,770 --> 00:02:59,990
I used to live in Barcelona, which is quite different to London because want it has a beach and the sea on one side and on the other side.

33
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:14,350
It has mountains so it's contained by nature and you can get to the nature quite quickly, which is really nice what about you have you lived anywhere different Yeah, I've lived in a few big cities.

34
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:27,970
A few capital cities, actually, I've also lived in Spain, but in Madrid, I lived and worked in Prague, and that is a really pretty.

35
00:03:27,970 --> 00:03:29,230
It's a beautiful city.

36
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:33,000
Yeah, the architecture looks fantastic.

37
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,460
Nice buildings, talking about nice buildings.

38
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:43,580
I lived in Edinburgh 'cause I did my master's degree there, and that has. Beautiful buildings.

39
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,320
I loved that city.

40
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:51,260
It has a castle on a big rock in the middle, and it's just amazing to look at.

41
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:53,000
So we've talked about cities.

42
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,380
We've been to.

43
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:55,760
What about the future.

44
00:03:55,810 --> 00:04:04,360
Are there any cities you really want to visit or maybe even live in? Oh, that's an interesting question.

45
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:11,500
I've never been to. Georgia or Armenia or that part of the world.

46
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:16,120
So I'm going to say I'd like to go to Tbilisi in Georgia.

47
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,140
That's a good answer.

48
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:18,940
I'd love to go there as well.

49
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:26,650
For me, I'm desperate to go to. Latin America, I really want to go to Rio de Janeiro.

50
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:33,910
And at the time when the carnival is there because that sounds really fun and I liked party.

51
00:04:33,910 --> 00:04:47,080
Let's recap the vocabulary we heard during the conversation, starting with bustling, which means busy.

52
00:04:47,090 --> 00:04:52,280
With lots of people and activity, we also heard convenient.

53
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:57,020
If something is convenient, it means it's very easy to do it.

54
00:04:57,020 --> 00:05:00,980
For example, there's lots of public transport in London.

55
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:03,280
So it's convenient for travel.

56
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:11,860
And we talked about possible plans for the future using would like to. For example, I'd like to visit Tbilisi in Georgia.

57
00:05:11,910 --> 00:05:20,100
That's it for this episode of real easy English, but we'll be back next week with another conversation in easy English.

58
